WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:01.680
My name's Penny Jarrett,

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:05.520
I'm a business developer,
youth mentor and blogger

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.560
and I have ADHD which is attention
deficit hyperactive disorder.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:21.280
ADHD is a mental disorder
which causes behavioural issues.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:25.320
A lot of people think that people
with ADHD can't pay attention

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.240
but the thing is, is we can
just pay too much attention

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.480
so paying attention to the wrong
things or a lot of things at once.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.240
Sometimes I feel like
I've got eight brains

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.560
and each one has 40 tabs open.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:39.360
I can be talking to someone

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:43.440
and then another tab opens and I just
start thinking about something else

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:44.600
and I give it my full attention,

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:47.040
like I feel like I have
to give it my full attention,

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.480
for like three seconds.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.680
People with ADHD
have a lot of energy.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.360
So there's a lot of fidgeting,
we can't keep still.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.440
We usually have
struggles following instructions.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:58.480
We get distracted a lot,

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.160
so it means that
we don't finish things

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:02.760
and sometimes
don’t even start things.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.480
There are loads of good things
about ADHD too.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.560
So an ADHD brain is usually creative,

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:11.920
there are loads
of artists, comedians...

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:15.360
singers, yeah,
there's loads of creatives.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:19.160
We've got great imaginations
which lead to a good sense of humour,

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:20.280
so we're funny.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:25.480
And I think that's a lot to do with
just doing funny things all the time,

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.080
like I sometimes
find my remote in the fridge.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:32.000
Managing ADHD includes
managing your environment

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.840
so you're not always gonna
have control over where you are.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:39.440
For instance, if I'm in a white room,
just completely bland,

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:43.360
I find that I start getting
breathless and panicky

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:46.720
and looking around
and just can't focus on anything.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:50.560
But if I'm somewhere
which is colourful and vibrant,

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:51.520
I feel calm.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.600
And I think that's why my house
is quite colourful,

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.000
I didn’t realise it before

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:58.960
but when I got diagnosed I looked
around me and I was like, "OK".

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:04.200
Managing and holding down
a normal nine to five job is mad.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:05.840
I've even walked out of meetings,

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.320
I've been in meeting rooms and
just had the urge to just walk out.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.760
I didn’t even notice until I was
halfway down the corridor that,

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.040
"Was I just in a meeting?"

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:15.640
It's just the brain under-stimulated,

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.560
it just searches for stimulation
in any way

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.640
and if that has to be
outside of that room

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.800
then yeah, meetings getting left.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:26.120
When I'm selling to customers
on the phone,

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:30.080
I make affirmation cards,
handmade with Sharpies and pencils,

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:32.240
and they have positive words on.

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:34.520
Things that I can
look at and remember

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.800
when I'm having anxious thoughts
or just not feeling good.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.400
Even if I'm not trying to focus
on something in particular,

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:42.680
like a phone call,

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.560
I need to be changing what I'm doing

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.720
so that I can give enough
energy to all my tasks.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:52.960
So if I had a to do list
with ten things on it for the day

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:57.480
where a neuro-typical person
might do each one at a time,

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.920
maybe even put
them in order of priority,

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.560
I can't always figure out
which one I should prioritise

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:05.960
and that's interesting actually

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:10.320
because people with ADHD have
an interest-based nervous system

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.680
so, yeah, we find prioritising hard.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:16.480
If I timebox myself and
give 15 minutes to each thing

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:17.760
and keep coming back

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:22.040
then I'm stimulated enough
to complete all of them

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.680
and at a high level.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:29.360
I was only diagnosed with ADHD
last year, when I was 30.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:32.920
So at first it was
such a negative to me.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.680
After doing a lot of research,

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:37.720
I stopped feeling negative
about ADHD

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.600
because I learnt about
all the good things.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:44.720
The best thing about having
ADHD, I think, is hyperfocus.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:45.960
And what that means is that

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:49.440
we can actually zone in
to that thing for several hours

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:51.280
and it not feel like several hours

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:54.960
and we go in so hard,
masterpieces come out of it.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.840
And that's why a lot of creatives

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:00.680
they master what they do
if they've got ADHD

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.760
because when hyperfocus kicks in
nothing will distract you.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:07.200
Not even hunger or sleep.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:11.680
ADHD is manageable so it
doesn’t have to remain negative,

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:14.960
and it doesn’t have to
define you in a negative way.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:18.120
The symptoms of ADHD
are with me, and always will be,

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:21.160
but they don’t have to define me
in a negative way.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:25.000
If I learn how to manage my ADHD
then I learn how to manage my life.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:28.000
And I can be just as productive
and successful as I want.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.160
Just not every single day.

